{"iDo":{"cfu":"Teacher says: 'My name is Sana. I am 6 years old.' Class shows two fingers for two details, then says both together.","steps":[{"n":1,"say":"Our strategy is Listen — Remember — Say It Back. I listen with quiet ears first. Then I hold the words in my mind.","action":"Point to Pinky in the first panel on p.3. Read 'My name is Pinky. I am 6 years old' slowly once.","sayLocal":"Hamari strategy hai Listen — Remember — Say It Back. Pehle chup ho kar sunta/sunti hoon, phir words yaad rakhta/rakhti hoon."},{"n":2,"say":"I heard 'Pinky' so I remember her name. I heard '6 years old' so I remember her age.","action":"Point to the same words on the page as you say them again. Children hold up one finger for 'name', two fingers for 'age'.","sayLocal":"Main ne 'Pinky' suna to naam yaad raha. '6 years old' suna to age yaad rahi."},{"n":3,"say":"Now I say both details back politely: 'Hello, Pinky. You are 6 years old.'","action":"Point to Pinky's waving picture while saying the full response. Children say it together with you once.","sayLocal":"Ab main dono details ke saath polite jawab deta/deti hoon: 'Hello, Pinky. You are 6 years old.'"}],"keyFact":"A good listener says both details back: the name AND the detail heard.","minutes":6,"ifStruggle":"Say only the name first, let children echo just 'Pinky', then add '6 years old' as a second small step.","teacherSays":"Listen — Remember — Say It Back: hear the words, hold them, then answer with the name and the detail.","cfuPassSignal":"Children's choral answer has both the name and the detail, not just one word.","teacherSaysLocal":"Listen — Remember — Say It Back: words suno, yaad rakho, phir naam aur detail dono ke saath jawab do."},"cost":0,"goal":"Listen to a speaker, remember the details, and say them back in a polite response.","hook":{"story":"Point to Pinky waving on p.3. She has a sign behind her and a paintbrush in another picture. Ask: what will she tell us about herself?","warmUp":{"teacherAsks":"Whole class: clap once when you hear a greeting, stay still for a name. 'Hello' — 'Pinky' — 'Good morning' — 'Jojo.'","expectedAnswer":"Clap for Hello/Good morning; stay still for Pinky/Jojo."},"keyWords":[{"term":"name","def":"The word used to call a person.","urdu":"نام"},{"term":"listen","def":"Keep ears and mind ready for another person's words.","urdu":"سننا"},{"term":"respond","def":"Answer politely using a detail you heard.","urdu":"جواب دینا"}],"minutes":3},"meta":{"day":2,"grade":1,"topic":"Recognise sounds, words","total":8,"isUrdu":true,"minutes":30,"subject":"english","comingUp":[{"day":3,"pages":"","topic":"Attempt to express feelings and ideas"},{"day":4,"pages":"7","topic":"Take turns to speak"},{"day":5,"pages":"8","topic":"Identify one-syllable words that rhyme"},{"day":6,"pages":"10-11","topic":"Name various objects"},{"day":7,"pages":"2-11","topic":"Chapter assessment (worksheet)"},{"day":8,"pages":"2-11","topic":"Chapter revision day"}],"cpaPhase":"","lessonId":"grade_1_english_ch1_seg2","materials":["textbook pp.3-4","notebook","pencil"],"skillType":"reading_comprehension","sourceFile":"~/Documents/Projects/April 2026/Rumi 10 April 2026/06_Logs & Misc/Reports/Active/Simulation Week - July 2026/ICT/Curriculum Ingestion (Taleemabad K-5)/03_enrichment/grade_1_english/grade_1_english_ch1_seg2.json","urduMedium":false,"designNotes":"Comic passage; literal comprehension of Pinky's intro.","durationMin":30,"chapterTitle":"Textbook pp.3-4","journeySoFar":[{"day":1,"pages":"2","topic":"Pronounce familiar one-syllable words"}],"pagesPrinted":[3,4],"teacherGender":"woman","sloDescriptions":["Recognise sounds, words or phrases in the language and repeat them","Listen to others and respond appropriately"]},"weDo":{"cfu":"What does Pinky do after school? Show one finger for school, two for park.","action":"Sound out and read p.3's school-and-park lines together, word by word, then say the detail-and-response pattern as a class.","minutes":9,"strategy":"Read 'This is my school' slowly, sound each word, children echo. Read 'After school, I go to the park' the same way. Point to the paintbrush picture: ask which word matches it ('paint'). Together say: 'Pinky paints in the park' as one class response.","modelled":{"problem":"p.3: what does Pinky do after school?","work":["'This is my school. I learn new things.'","'After school, I go to the park.'","'I paint in the park.' — matches the paintbrush picture"],"answer":"She goes to the park after school and paints there."}},"wrap":{"homework":["p.4: tell a family member 'My name is ___. I like to ___.'","p.3 question: ask them 'What do you like doing?' and listen to their answer"],"keyFacts":["Listen — Remember — Say It Back: answer with the detail you heard.","A polite response repeats the speaker's name and one detail."],"exitOptions":[{"form":"mcq","prompt":"A friend says: 'I live in G-9.' Which answer shows you listened?","choices":["Hello! You live in G-9.","I like mangoes.","What is your name?","Hello, goodbye!"],"correct":"A","promptLocal":"Dost kehta hai: 'I live in G-9.' Kaun sa jawab batata hai ke tum ne suna?","howToRun":"Read the question and all four choices aloud twice. Children show A, B, C or D on fingers together."},{"form":"short","prompt":"Listen: 'My name is Omar. I like cricket.' Say back both details together as a class.","answer":"'Hello, Omar. You like cricket.'","howToRun":"Say the line twice, then signal the whole class to answer together in one voice."}],"minutes":3},"bloom":"understand","youDo":{"action":"Each child works alone on p.4 Activity 1, filling in their own name line. Check together at the end with thumbs up.","minutes":9,"behind":{"prompt":"Trace or copy your own name on the Activity 1 line, then say 'My name is ___' aloud when asked.","answer":"Own name written; says name aloud with help if needed.","coach":"Point to the line, say the child's name slowly, let them trace/write it, then say it with them once."},"ahead":{"prompt":"Fill in all five Activity 1 blanks on p.4 about yourself, then whisper your full introduction once silently.","answer":"All five lines filled with own name, age, place, subject, and activity."},"problems":[{"n":1,"ref":"p.4 Activity 1","prompt":"Write your own name on line 1: 'My name is ___.'","answer":"Own name written."},{"n":2,"ref":"p.4 Activity 1","prompt":"Write your own age on line 2: 'I am ___ years old.'","answer":"Own age written."},{"n":3,"ref":"p.4 Activity 1","prompt":"Write where you live on line 3: 'I live in ___.'","answer":"Own town/area written."},{"n":4,"ref":"p.4 Activity 1","prompt":"Write what you like to do on line 5: 'I like to do ___.'","answer":"Own activity written."}]},"sloCode":"E-01-RD-01","sloFull":"By the end of the lesson, students will recognise sounds, words or phrases in the language and repeat them, and listen to others and respond appropriately.","totalMinutes":30}
