{"meta":{"lessonId":"grade_1_english_ch10_seg4","grade":1,"subject":"english","language":"en","topic":"Opposites: Job Talk / Opposite Day (Antonyms)","chapterTitle":"Ch.10 · Pinky's Garden of Wonders!","minutes":40,"sloDescriptions":["Opposite words mean the other way: Found—Lost, Small—Big, Sad—Happy, Sunny—Cloudy."],"source":"v9_html","adapterV2":2},"goal":"Opposite words mean the other way: Found—Lost, Small—Big, Sad—Happy, Sunny—Cloudy.","sloFull":"Opposite words mean the other way: Found—Lost, Small—Big, Sad—Happy, Sunny—Cloudy.","sloCode":"E-01-VG-21","hook":{"minutes":4,"warmUp":{"teacherAsks":"Look at p.132. What fun day does the page name?","expectedAnswer":"Opposite Day"},"steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Hold up the textbook open to p.132 and point to the two children in the speech bubble."},{"n":2,"action":"Read the bubble aloud: \"Guess what day it is? It's Opposite Day!\""},{"n":3,"action":"Ask the whole class together: \"Found — what word means the other way?\" Children call out the answer together."},{"n":4,"say":"Aaj hum opposite (ulta) alfaz dhoondenge — jaise Found ka ulta Lost."}],"cfu":"Whole class calls out: is 'opposite' the same word or the other way word? (Answer: the other way.)"},"iDo":{"minutes":8,"steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Point to the word 'Found' on p.132 and say: 'This word needs its opposite.'"},{"n":2,"say":"Found... the word that means the other way is Lost. Found—Lost."},{"n":3,"action":"Point to 'Small' on the page and think aloud: 'Small is little, so the other way is Big.' Say the pair: Small—Big."},{"n":4,"action":"Show writing the answer neatly on the line next to 'Found' and 'Small' in the book, saying: 'Main yeh jawab line par likhta hoon.'"}],"cfu":"Whole class, thumbs up if Found—Lost is correct, thumbs down if not."},"weDo":{"minutes":12,"strategy":"Group children by row/level. Each row gets one word pair to work out with choral answers before anyone writes.","steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Front rows (sound/letter level): look at 'Sad' on p.132, say the word aloud together, then choral-call the opposite 'Happy' after a teacher prompt."},{"n":2,"action":"Middle rows (word level): look at 'Sunny' on p.132, discuss in their row which word means the other way, then call out 'Cloudy' together."},{"n":3,"action":"Back rows (sentence level, ahead): say the full pair as a sentence together — 'Sunny is the opposite of Cloudy because they mean the other way' — then whisper-check with their row before the teacher confirms."}],"cfu":"Teacher calls each row in turn; row answers together in one chorus voice."},"youDo":{"minutes":12,"steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Each child writes the two remaining opposite pairs (Sad—Happy, Sunny—Cloudy) alone on the p.132 lines in their own book."},{"n":2,"action":"Children who finish early (ahead) also write one new opposite pair of their own choosing, such as Hot—Cold, in their copy."}],"problems":[{"n":1,"prompt":"Textbook p.132: Sad ______","answer":"Sad — Happy."},{"n":2,"prompt":"Textbook p.132: Sunny ______","answer":"Sunny — Cloudy."}],"cfu":"Whole class holds up their open book together to show the written pairs."},"wrap":{"minutes":4,"exitOptions":[{"prompt":"Whole class, say it together: what is the opposite of Hot?","answer":"Cold — whole class calls this out together."}],"homework":["Say the four opposite pairs from p.132 to a family member: Found—Lost, Small—Big, Sad—Happy, Sunny—Cloudy."]}}
