":"Teacher reads it back slowly; children self-check their own copy as each word is said."},{"n":4,"action":"Point to 'well-known' (hyphen), 'lamb' (silent letter), 'trying' (-y word) and say: this one sentence uses all three spells you need today."}],"cfu":"Ask whole class together: “Which word has a silent letter, and which letter is silent?” Expect: lamb, the b."},"weDo":{"minutes":12,"strategy":"Row-groups by level, each builds its own small word bank and topic sentence; choral check at the end of each round.","steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Row A (ahead): build a word bank of 3 words (1 hyphenated, 1 -e/-y transform, 1 silent-letter) for their own theme, unaided. Row B (on-level): choose from teacher-given word options (well-known / trying / knee) to build their bank. Row C (needs support): use the word bank already on p.42 (well-known, trying, lamb)."},{"n":2,"action":"Each row says its topic sentence together, choral, once ready: 'My theme is ___. My topic sentence is ___.'"},{"n":3,"action":"Whole class checks each row's sentence: thumbs up if it names the theme clearly and uses a word-bank word."}],"cfu":"Whole class choral: “Does this topic sentence name ONE clear theme?” — thumbs up/down."},"youDo":{"minutes":12,"steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Everyone: in your copy, write your topic sentence plus at least 2 body sentences about your own theme, using your word bank."},{"n":2,"action":"Ahead children: add a fourth skill not required — a contraction or a relative pronoun — in one of your sentences."}],"problems":[{"n":1,"prompt":"Circle the silent letter in each: know, climb, knee, lamb."},{"n":2,"prompt":"Write your paragraph: topic sentence + 3-5 body sentences + concluding sentence, using your word bank."}],"cfu":"Ask two pupils to read their topic sentence aloud; whole class says the theme back together."},"wrap":{"minutes":4,"exitOptions":[{"prompt":"Hold up your copy. Point to one word-bank word in your topic sentence and be ready to name its spell: hyphen, -e/-y